		<methods>
			<methodStep>
				<description>
					<section>
						<title></title>
						<para>We performed a field census to assess tree health within the 35-ha ForestGEO plot. This census involves conducting comprehensive visual examinations of all stems greater than 10 cm in diameter, focusing on indicators such as canopy condition, pests and pathogens, and physical damages. These field observations were meticulously recorded to create a detailed dataset capturing the health status of individual trees across the study area.</para>
					</section>
				</description>
			</methodStep>
		</methods>
